Some few-shot examples may be useful:
Query:
--Description: 1)  Look at patients that have “bad-history” or “redaction” annotations.
SELECT DISTINCT
  `case_barcode`,
  `category`  AS annotation_category,
  `classification` AS annotation_classification
FROM `isb-cgc.TCGA_bioclin_v0.Annotations`
WHERE entity_type = 'Patient'
  AND (category = 'History of unacceptable prior treatment related to a prior/other malignancy'
       OR classification = 'Redaction')
LIMIT 20;
Answer:
case_barcode,annotation_category,annotation_classification
TCGA-P6-A5OG,History of unacceptable prior treatment related to a prior/other malignancy,Notification
TCGA-5L-AAT1,History of unacceptable prior treatment related to a prior/other malignancy,Notification
TCGA-A8-A084,History of unacceptable prior treatment related to a prior/other malignancy,Notification
Query:
--Description: 2)  Young (≤30 yrs), female BRCA patients in TCGA clinical table.
SELECT DISTINCT
  `case_barcode`
FROM `isb-cgc.TCGA_bioclin_v0.Clinical`
WHERE UPPER(gender) = 'FEMALE'
  AND disease_code = 'BRCA'
  AND age_at_diagnosis <= 30
LIMIT 20;
